"hadiths[192]{hadithnumber,text}:"
4050,"Ibn Abu Malikah says: I met Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubayr at that time, he was riding a mule from Qaiqaan. I inquired what is your opinion about such a person. He who divorces his wife three times, he said: Sayyiduna Uthman (RA) has appointed such a woman as an heir."
4051,"Talha bin Abdullah narrates: Sayyidna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) declared Tamazar bint Asbagh as the heir of Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with him), although Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) divorced this woman, he divorced her during his illness."
4052,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates: People found this in the letter of Sayyidna 'Umar (RA) that when someone commits a sin, his guardian should divorce him on his behalf."
4053,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates: We have found this in the letter of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr. ""When a madman commits adultery with his wife, his guardian should divorce him on his behalf."""
4054,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) says: When a madman commits adultery with his wife, his guardian will be ordered to divorce him."
4055,"Muhammad bin Makhlad informed us, Sulayman bin Tawbah informed us, Abu Hudhayfah informed us."
4056,"Saeed Bin Musayyib narrates: An Arab slave girl ran away, she reached the Qura Valley, she reached the tribe from whom she ran away, a man from Banu Zara married her, she had many children, then the master of this slave girl came to him, he wanted to take custody of this slave girl and her children. As a ransom, a slave (or yaknes) should be paid, a male slave for a boy and a female slave for a girl, if these are not available, the townspeople will pay 60 dinars or 700 dirhams for a slave, and six duties will be imposed on the villagers."
4057,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says about (declaring) haram, it is an oath for which expiation must be made."
4058,"Saeed bin Musayb, Ata, Taaws, Sulayman bin Yasar, and Saeed bin Jubeer say: (Declaring) forbidden is an oath for which expiation will be paid."
4059,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Acquire the knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people because it is half of knowledge and it is the first thing that will be forgotten and it is the first thing that will be taken away from my ummah."
4060,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that there are three types of knowledge, and what is in addition to that is extra."
4061,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this after the revelation of Surah Nisa and the rules of inheritance were revealed in it."
4062,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said: No one can be held captive from the shares of inheritance appointed by Allah. Except for Ibn Lahiyyah, no one has narrated its chain of transmission, he has narrated it on the authority of his brother. Both narrators are weak."
4063,"Sayyiduna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, has said this about (the deceased's) two daughters, mother, father and wife."
4064,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: One religion does not become the heir of another religion and the testimony of people belonging to one religion cannot be accepted against another religion. And the narrator named Umar is Umar bin Rashid who is not authentic."
4065,"Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): No unbeliever can inherit from a Muslim, and no Muslim can inherit from an unbeliever."
4066,"Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: I was standing under the camel of the Prophet (PBUH) at that time, and its saliva was flowing over me. On that occasion, he said, ""Allah has determined the right of every rightful owner, therefore, a will cannot be made for an heir. The offspring will be a slave and the adulterer will be deprived. No one will be called by anyone other than his father. Do not attribute it to anyone other than the one who does it. The person who does this will be cursed by Allah continuously. A woman should not spend anything in her husband's house without his permission. A person said, O Messenger of Allah! Not even cereal? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “It is our most important wealth.” After that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “The thing given as a loan must be returned."
4067,"These are the words in another hadith, Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I stood under the camel of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4068,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Pay the property according to the obligatory parts of the inheritance, and whatever property is left over, it will belong to the next of kin."
4069,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Divide the property between the obligatory shares, whatever remains after the obligatory shares will belong to a close male relative. Abu Shiba narrated these words: Distribute the inheritance among the Dhu al-Faruz according to the order of the Book of Allah."
4070,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Give the obligatory shares to their sharers, and whoever is left will be taken by a close relative."
4071,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace: Give the obligatory portion to those who are entitled to it, and whatever remains will be given to a close relative."
4072,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: Divide the wealth according to the obligatory parts, and whatever is left will be given to a close male relative."
4073,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: Divide the property according to the obligatory parts, and whatever remains will be given to a close relative."
4074,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood up and said: People belonging to two religions will not inherit each other. If so, that woman will not inherit anything from that man's property and wealth, and if one of them has killed the other as a sin, then he will inherit the property, but not the property. The narrator of this tradition is Muhammed bin Saeed Ta'ifi Thaqa."
4075,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4076,"It is narrated about Umar bin Abdul Aziz that he did not declare any deceased as the heir of another deceased, he only declared living persons as heirs of the deceased."
4077,"Shaykh Abul Zanad narrates: In the event of Hura, the inheritance of those who were killed was divided, so the living were made heirs of the deceased, and the deceased were not made heirs of each other."
4078,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: A woman named Umm Kulthum and her son Zayd, who was the son of Sayyidna Umar (RA) both died at the same time, but it was not known which of them died first. So they did not become the heirs of Ekad Vasra."
4079,"Ayyas bin Abd has the honor of being a companion (he says) when their house fell on some people, they were made heirs of each other."
4080,"It is narrated that Iyas bin Abd was asked about a house that is going to fall on people and those people die, so he said that those people will inherit each other."
4081,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: No Muslim can inherit from a Christian, except if he (a Christian) is his (Muslim) slave or slave (he will become an heir)."
4082,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) states: A Jew or a Christian cannot inherit from a Muslim, and a Muslim will not inherit from these people, but if he is a Jew or a Christian Muslim's (slave) or his slave (then the ruling will be different)."
4083,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this as the above hadith: (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said) We cannot inherit from the People of the Book and they cannot inherit from us, but a person can inherit from his (people of the Book) slaves or women."
4084,"Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People belonging to different religions cannot inherit from each other. You have also said this: The woman will inherit from her husband's wealth and his wealth, and the man will also inherit from the wealth of this woman, but if one of them kills the other, if he killed his partner intentionally, then he will not inherit from his property, and he will not inherit in wealth, but if the deceased was killed by mistake, then (on the other hand) he will inherit from his property, but in wealth. He will not inherit anything."
4085,"The same hadith along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4086,"Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) wrote in a letter to Sayyidna Dahhak Bin Sufyan (RA) that he should make Sayyidna Ashim Al-Adhabi the wife of his heirs."
4087,"It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Mughira bin Shuba, may Allah be pleased with him, that he narrates: Zarara bin Majli, or perhaps Haran, said to Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote in a letter to Sayyidna Dahhak bin Sufyan, that he should be declared the heir, after that, according to a previous tradition. This tradition has also been copied by other narrators."
4088,"Sayyidna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu says: Sayyidna Ashim was killed as a mistake."
4089,"Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, stood up and inquired whether any of you have any knowledge about whether the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave any decision regarding the inheritance of a woman in the death of a murdered husband. On this matter, Sayyiduna Dahhak bin Sufyan (RA) said, ""I have knowledge about this. The Prophet (PBUH) wrote us this letter that we should give Ashim Zababi's wife a share of her husband's dowry."""
4090,"Saeed bin Musayb, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab, may God be pleased with him, said: I think that the dowry will be given only to the Asaba relatives, because these are the people who also pay the dowry. After that, the narrator has narrated the hadith according to the previous one, and the names also contain the words that Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) gave a decision according to it. A narrator named Ibn Jaraj has quoted these words additionally."
4091,"Saeed bin Musaib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab said that the dowry will be given to the family members and a woman will not inherit anything from her husband's dowry, until Sayyidna Dahhak bin Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) told him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote this letter to me."
4092,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib Radiyallahu Anhu says: According to the duties prescribed by Allah Ta'ala, the inheritance will be divided and the heir will share in it."
4093,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were on a journey with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until Aswaf, we came to a woman who was the grandmother of Al-Khaz bin Zayd. We stayed with her that day. They are the daughters of Saeed bin Rabi who were martyred with you in the Battle of Uhud. Their uncle has taken over their property and their share of inheritance. The two cannot marry, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Allah will decide about this."" Then the verse of Surah Nisa was revealed in which this command is given: ""Allah has decreed about your offspring that the share of one male will be equal to that of two females."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me, call this woman to me and bring her other half as well. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the executor of these girls: You give two-thirds of the inheritance to these girls and one-eighth to their mother, and you will get the remainder."
4094,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned one-eighth share to his wife, two-thirds share to his two daughters, and the remaining wealth to his brother-in-law."
4095,"Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Sa’d bin Rabi’ (may Allah be pleased with him) came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and she said, “O Messenger of Allah, Sayyidna Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred with him (after that, the narrator has mentioned the entire hadith in which these words are mentioned). You will get the baby."
4096,"Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The wife of Sayyidna Sa’d Bin Rabi’ (RA) said: O Messenger of Allah, Sayyidna Sa’d (RA) has passed away. He left two daughters and a brother. He did not answer, then she came to his service and said, O Messenger of Allah, it is the matter of the two daughters of Sayyiduna Sa'd, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Call his brother to Mir."" When that person came, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, ""Give two-thirds to his daughters and one-eighth to his wife, and you will get what is left over."""
4097,"Sayyidna Huzail bin Shahrabeel narrates: A man came to Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari and Salman bin Rabi'ah, and he inquired from them about the inheritance of a daughter, a granddaughter, and a half-sister. They both said: The daughter will get half of the property, and the rest of the wealth will go to her sister. The person who will answer according to our opinion came to Sayyidna Abdullah, asked him about it and told him that both of them had given this answer, then Sayyidna Abdullah said, I will give the decision about this that was given by the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, half of the daughter will get, the sixth part will be given to the granddaughter, so that two-thirds will be completed, and the rest of the wealth will be given to her sister."
4098,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4099,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4100,"Huzail bin Shahrabeel narrates: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari was asked about a person who leaves behind a daughter, a granddaughter, and a half-sister. Hazrat Abu Musa said that his daughter will get half of it, and the rest of the property will be given to his sister. I said: Yes, the people asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud about this and told them about the answer of Sayyiduna Abu Musa al-Ash’ari, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud said, “How can I say this when I heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) saying that (in such a situation) the daughter will get half, the granddaughter will get a sixth, thus two-thirds of the shares will be completed and the remainder will be given to the sister-in-law. will be found."
4101,"Imam Jafar Sadiq narrates this statement of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir): Umm Kulthum, the daughter of Sayyidna Ali (RA) and her (wife) son Zayd (who was the son of Sayyidna Umar RA) both of them died on the same day. So that woman did not become the heir of this child and that child did not become the heir of this woman, similarly the people of Safin did not become the heirs of each other, in the same way the people who were killed in the incident of Hara did not become the heirs of each other."
4102,"Shaykh Abu Hani Umar bin Bashir says: Sayyidna Aamir (RA) was asked about a child who is neither male nor female, nor does it have any signs of a male, nor does it have any signs of a female, but urine or faeces comes out of his navel."
4103,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to me: Acquire the knowledge of the Qur’an and teach it to the people. Acquire the knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people. Acquire knowledge and teach it to the people, because I will pass away and soon the knowledge will be taken away and temptations will begin to appear. can decide between The same raiyat is also quoted in some other isnads."
4104,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Acquire knowledge and teach it to the people; “Acquire knowledge of inheritance and teach it to the people; Couldn't decide between the two."
4105,"Saeed bin Hasan narrates: I said to Sufyan al-Thawri: If you take the position of giving a decision about inheritance, from whom will you seek guidance in this regard? So Sufyan replied: (I will be guided by the rulings) regarding the inheritance of Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit."
4106,"Aswad bin Yazid narrates that Sayyidna Mu'adhbin Jabal, may Allah be pleased with him, came to us at the time when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, had sent him."
4107,"Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates that Sayyidna Umar bin Khattab (RA) gave half of the share to his daughter and gave the remaining property to her."
4108,"Aswad bin Yazid Kufi narrates that Sayyidna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) divided the inheritance of a person in Yemen who left behind a daughter and a sister. Sayyidna Mu'adh (RA) gave half to his daughter and half to his sister."
4109,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the slave of Sayyidna Hamza (RA) died, leaving behind a daughter and a daughter of Sayyidna Hamza (RA), so the Prophet (PBUH) gave half a share to the daughter of that slave and also gave half a share to the daughter of Sayyidna Hamza (RA)."
4110,"Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: My son has passed away, what will I get from his inheritance? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will get a sixth. When he went back, he called him and said: You will get another sixth. When he went back, the Prophet called him and said: You will get another sixth in addition."
4111,"Sayyidna Abu Umamah bin Sahl Hanif (RA) narrates that a person killed another person with a crossbow. This person was only his uncle. Sayyidna Abu Ubaidah Bin Jarrah (RA) wrote a letter about this to Sayyidna Umar (RA). There are mullahs and the person who has no heir, his maternal uncle will become his heir."
4112,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Verily, whoever has no guardian, Allah is his guardian, and whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle will inherit him."
4113,"Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: He who has no guardian, Allah is his guardian, and he who has no heir, his maternal uncle will inherit him. Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Allah and His Messenger will be the guardians of the person who has no guardian, and the maternal uncle will be the heir of the person who has no heir."
4114,"Shaykh Abu Asim was asked whether this was narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he remained silent. So Shazkuni said to him: Tell us a hadith about the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him. So he remained silent."
4115,"This tradition is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, this tradition is ""suspended""."
4116,"Sayyiduna Muqadam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: I am closer to every believer than his life, whoever leaves property, it will be given to his heirs, and whoever leaves debt or children (even if they are not in a happy state), then they will come to me. Who has no heir because he will pay off his debt and fulfill his obligations."
4117,"The same tradition and chain of transmission is narrated by Sayyidna Muqadam bin Maad Yakarb (RA)."
4118,"This tradition is transmitted as a ""suspended"" tradition along with another document."
4119,"This tradition is transmitted as a ""suspended"" tradition along with another document."
4120,"The same hadith is narrated from Sayyida Aisha on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: Allah and His Messenger (are his guardians)."
4121,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: ""Whoever has no heir, his maternal uncle becomes the heir."""
4122,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this saying of the Prophet (PBUH): The maternal uncle becomes the heir."
4123,"Alqamah has narrated this about Abdul Malik that when a person has a grandchild and a niece, then the wealth will be divided between them by half. It is true that this is Alqamah's own opinion."
4124,"Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: You recite the commandment of the will before paying the debt while reciting. But the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Before the will (of the deceased) is fulfilled, the debt will be paid and siblings from the mother's side will inherit from each other, while siblings from the father's side will not inherit from each other."
4125,"Al-Harith narrates that a case came to Sayyidna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) about two cousins, one of whom was a half-brother on the mother's side. If I were in his place, I would have given him one-sixth and divided the remaining wealth among them (other cousins)."
4126,"Masoud bin Haqm al-Saqfi narrates that a case came to Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with her, which was about a woman who left behind her husband, her mother, maternal siblings, and paternal siblings. Had not made the other a sharer', then Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: The decision we gave at that time was that of that time. Our decision today is what we have given now."
4127,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) made his Companions brothers, then they made each other heirs, until this verse was revealed: ""Only (lineal) relatives will inherit each other."" After that, people started to inherit each other according to lineage."
4128,"Sayyiduna Wathila bin Asqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: A woman inherits from three people: from her freed (slave) her children and from her child whom she cursed."
4129,"Sayyidna Wathla bin Asqaa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: A woman inherits in three ways: the inheritance of her freed (slave or maidservant) whom she raised (i.e. fostering an abandoned child), her inheritance and the one for whom she cursed."
4130,"This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Wasila (RA) along with another chain of transmission."
4131,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) ordered three grandmothers and grandmothers to pay one-sixth of it."
4132,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates that two grandmothers (namely, Yadadi and Nani) came to Sayyidna Abu Bakr, so Sayyidna Abu Bakr named Nani instead of the grandmother, and Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl said to them: 'They have participated in the Battle of Badr.' O Caliph Messenger! You have given the inheritance to her so that if she dies, she (the woman) will not be her heir."
4133,"Qasim bin Muhammad narrates that a grandmother and a grandmother came to the service of Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Radi Allahu Anhu). There was a grandmother and a grandmother. So Sayyidna Abu Bakr (Radi Allahu Anhu) ordered to pay the legacy to the grandmother. He did not order for the grandmother. Abd al-Rahman bin Sahl, who belonged to Banu Haritha, said to him: O Caliph Messenger! You have ordered to pay it so that if she died, she would not be his heir, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) ordered to pay both of them (the narrator says:) i.e. ordered to pay one-sixth part."
4134,"Abdullah bin Baridah narrates from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had ordered the grandmother to pay one-sixth of the share while there was no mother below her."
4135,"Sayyidna Muaqal bin Yasar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave Nani (Yadadi) a sixth portion."
4136,"Ibrahim bin Yazid narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared three children as heirs, two of them were from the father's side and one was from the mother's side (that is, there were two grandmothers and one was a grandmother)."
4137,"Al-Khaari bin Zayd narrates this about his father Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA): He had inherited three valleys of grandmothers, while they were of the same rank, two of them from the father's side and one from the mother's side."
4138,"It has been narrated about Sayyidna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) that he named three wadis and grandmothers as heirs, of which two were from the maternal side and one was from the father's side."
4139,"Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) says: I testify about Sayyidna Abu Bakr Sadiq (RA) that he has given the status of grandfather and father."
4140,"Aqeel bin Khalid narrates: Saeed bin Sulaiman narrated to his father about his grandfather Zayd bin Thabit (RA) that once Sayyidna Umar (RA) asked for permission to enter his house. Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu said: O Commander of the Faithful! If you had sent me a message, 'I would have come to you', then Sayyidna Umar (RA) said: I have come to you on a mission, 'I have come to inquire about the ruling about Dada,' then Sayyidna Zayd (RA) said: 'No! By Allah! What is your opinion about this? So Sayyiduna Umar said: There is no revelation in this matter that we are guilty of any increase or decrease. This is a matter in which you have to give your opinion. If I understand that your opinion is in accordance with my opinion, then I will accept it. Otherwise, there will be no blame on you in this regard. He said: I have come here because you will solve my problem. Then Sayyiduna Umar came to Sayyidna Zayd again at the same time that he had come on the first day and discussed with him about it. Sayyidna Zayd said: I will give you something to write about this. So he wrote it on a piece of palan and explained it with an example. It grows on top of the stem, a branch comes out of it, then another branch comes out of it, that stem conveys the water to this branch, if the first branch is cut, the water will come to this branch, and if the second branch is cut, the water will go to the first branch. He said: I apply what Zayd has said about Dada. The narrator narrates: Sayyidna Umar (RA) was the first grandfather with whom this situation happened. He took all his wealth, that is, he took the property of his grandson and did not take the property of his sisters (i.e. granddaughters)."
4141,"It is narrated about Sayyiduna Umar (RA) that he had ruled that in the presence of siblings (of the deceased), the grandfather would also be a sharer, regardless of the number of siblings."
4142,"Yunus bin Yazid narrates that I inquired from Zuhri about the inheritance of a person who is survived by a grandfather and siblings. Zahri said: Saeed bin Musayb, Ubaidullah bin Abdullah and Qubaysa bin Zuayb have stated that Sayyidna Umar (RA) had given this decision: ""The grandfather will share with his siblings and the siblings from the father's side, while one-third of the wealth is better in his favor."" It will be given according to the calculation. They also gave this decision. Full-siblings have more rights than co-siblings from the father's side, whether they are male or female. However, if the co-siblings from the father's side are present with the full-siblings, then they will also get their share. If there is anything left after the obligatory share of the sisters, it will be given by the father to the co-brothers under the principle of equal share for one male and two female."
4143,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: A murderer will not inherit."
4144,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The murderer will not get anything (from the inheritance)."
4145,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA)."
4146,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH) that a murderer does not inherit."
4147,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer does not become an heir (of the murdered). Shaykh Abu Abd al-Rahman says: A narrator named Ishaq is an obsolete hadith."
4148,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A murderer will not inherit anything."
4149,"This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Amro bin Shuaib on the authority of his father on the authority of his grandfather."
4150,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
4151,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): “There can be no will for an heir."
4152,"Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The debt will be paid before the will is completed and no bequest will be made for the heir."
4153,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said: A will cannot be made for an heir."
4154,"Amro bin Shoaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this in his sermon on the Day of Sacrifice: A will cannot be made for an heir."
4155,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: It is not permissible to make a will for an heir, but if the other heirs wish (it can be done)."
4156,"Ata bin Yasarbayan says that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to Kurqaba on horseback so that he could discuss the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt, then Allah revealed the order that they would not inherit."
4157,"Sayyiduna Abd al-Rahman bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not received anything for him (i.e., I have not received any order to give him an inheritance)."
4158,"Hisham bin Arwah narrates on the authority of his father that Sayyiduna Zubair (RA) narrated that this verse was revealed to us: ""And the relatives will inherit each other (this is the order in the Book of Allah)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had made two Muhajirin and an Ansari brothers to each other, so we had no doubt that we would become each other's heirs. That is, if Sayyiduna Ka'b (R.A.) died and he had no heir, I thought that I would become his heir and if I died, he would also become my heir until this verse was revealed."
4159,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt, and he said, ""I do not know about it."" Gabriel will come (and tell me about it), then he said: Where is the person who inquires about the inheritance of his paternal grandmother and aunt? When this person was brought, he said: Gabriel has told me that these two will not get anything (i.e. they will not inherit). This hadith has been narrated only by a narrator named Masada with reference to Muhammad bin Amr, and this narrator is weak."
4160,"This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet along with another chain of transmission."
4161,"Sha'bi narrated: Ziyad bin Abu Sufyan said to his companion: Do you know what Sayyiduna Umar (RA) had decided about paternal aunt and paternal aunt? The man replied: No! Tuziad said: I know the best about what Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled in this regard."
4162,"Sayyidna Abu Baksha Anmari (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) conquered Makkah (i.e. attacked it), Sayyidna Zubair (RA) was in charge of the left part, while Sayyidna Muqdad (RA) was in charge of the right part. He removed the balloon and said: I have appointed two parts for the horse and one part for the rider."
4163,"Sayyiduna Abu Raham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I participated in an expedition with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and my brother was with me. We had two horses with us, so he gave us six shares."
4164,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned three parts to the rider and his horse: one part was for the man and two parts were for his horse."
4165,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) prescribed two parts for the horse and one part for the rider."
4166,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) assigned two shares for the horse and one share for the rider while dividing."
4167,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4168,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave three parts to a man and his horse: one part belonged to the man and two parts to his horse."
4169,"Sayyidna Muqdad Radiyallahu Anhu narrates that I participated in the Battle of Badr with the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam)."
4170,"Sayyidna Muqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me one share and two shares to my horse on the occasion of the Battle of Khyber."
4171,"Sayyidna Muqdad bin Amr (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Badr, the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to his horse and one part to him."
4172,"Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, Sayyidna Talha bin Ubaidullah and Sayyidna Zubair bin Awam (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave parts to a horse and a part to a man."
4173,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4174,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two hundred horses to two hundred horses on the occasion of the Battle of Hunain."
4175,"The same hadith is narrated along with another document which says: Every horse had two parts."
4176,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave one part to the horseman and two parts to the horse."
4177,"Bashir bin Umarubi says that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave four parts to my horse and one part to me, so I got five parts."
4178,"Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I participated in a battle with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
4179,"Sayyidna Majma bin Jariyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the occasion of the Battle of Hudaybiyyah. When we returned from there, people started running their camels. Some people asked others: What has happened to these people? We went out and found the Holy Prophet (PBUH) staying at the place of ""Kara' Al-Ghumayim"". When some people who were going towards him gathered there, the Prophet (PBUH) recited this verse: ""Verily, We have given you a clear victory."" The narrator narrates: So one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: Is this a victory? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes! Kind of this caste! In whose power is my life! This is victory. Narrator narrates: Then, among those who participated in the Hudaybiyah campaign, the property of the Khyber campaign was divided into eighteen parts. The number of the army was fifteen hundred, of which three were cavalrymen."
4180,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prescribed two parts for the horseman and one part for the footman. We have mentioned earlier."
4181,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates about the Prophet (PBUH) that he (PBUH) gave two parts to the cavalry and one part to the infantry."
4182,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave two shares to the horseman and one share to the footman. The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, the narrator has a doubt about one word whether that word is horse or horse."
4183,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4184,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the cavalry and one part to the infantry. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4185,"With another chain of transmission, it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be three parts for the horseman and one part for the footman."
4186,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) conquered Khyber, his (booty) was divided into eighteen parts."
4187,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair narrates the statement of Sayyidna Zubair, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me four shares on the day of the Battle of Badr, two shares were for my horse, one share was for me, and one share was for my mother, who was among the relatives."
4188,"Sayyiduna Zubair bin Al-Awam (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave him four parts: two parts were for his horse, one part was for him, and one part was for him, and one part was for his mother, who was among Dhu al-Qurbi."
4189,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates this on the authority of his father. He says: The Prophet (PBUH) gave four shares to Sayyidna Zubair Bin Awam (RA) on the day of the Battle of Khyber. One part was his, one part belonged to Dhu Al-Qurbi, who was Safiya bint Abdul Muttalib (i.e., who was the maternal grandmother of the Prophet (PBUH)) and two parts belonged to his horse (i.e. Sayyidna Zubair (RA))."
4190,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave four parts to Sayyidna Zubair (RA) one part was for his mother because of his qarat, one part was for Sayyidna Zubair (RA) and two parts were for his horse."
4191,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4192,"Muhammad bin Yahya narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father, 'He had accompanied the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Battle of Hunain, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given two parts to his horse and one part to him."
4193,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the horse and one part to the person with the horse."
4194,"Sayyidina Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave two parts to the horse and one part to the rider."
4195,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever puts a horse among two horses and is not sure that it will come out ahead, there is no harm in it, and whoever puts a horse in two horses and is sure that it will come out ahead, it is gambling."
4196,"Sayyidna Abu Saeed al-Khudri (RA) narrates that on the occasion of the Battle of Utas, we found some captive women, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: No one should have intercourse with a pregnant woman until she gives birth to her pregnancy, and a woman who is not pregnant should not have intercourse with her until she has menstruated once."
4197,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a slave leaves the kingdom of the polytheists before his master, he will be free, and if he leaves after his master, then he will be returned to the master. Will get back."
4198,"Salim bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever keeps his (former) wealth in the booty before the division of the booty, he will get it, and whoever finds it after the division of the booty, he will not get anything. The narrator named Ishaq is Ishaq bin Abu Farah and it is obsolete."
4199,"Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, says: The polytheists acquire the wealth of the Muslims, and then the Muslims prevail over them, then one of us finds his wealth with them, then he will be more entitled to this wealth than any other person. Shaykh Abu Sahl stated that he would be more entitled to receive this wealth in exchange for the price."
4200,"Salim narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The enemy who takes possession of the wealth and then before it is divided (into booty), if the owner of the wealth takes care of the wealth, it will be given to him."
4201,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The wealth that the enemy seizes and then the Muslims get that wealth from him, the original owner of that wealth can take it before it is divided, he will be more entitled to it. One of the narrators of this tradition, Hasan bin Amara, is extinct."
4202,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the day of Ghazwa Ahad, I was presented before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I was fourteen years old at that time. He did not allow me to participate. He did not consider me an adult. The narrator narrates: I told Sayyiduna Umar bin Abdul Aziz about this, so he wrote a letter to his government officials to pay the salary only to a person who has reached the age of fifteen. It was the custom of Sayyidna Umar bin Abdul Aziz that he fixed a salary of one hundred dirhams for a fifteen-year-old boy."
4203,"Sayyiduna Ya'la bin Marah (RA) narrates that I traveled with the Prophet (PBUH) many times, 'I saw you that whenever you passed by the dead body of a person, you did not pass on until you ordered him to be buried, you did not inquire whether it was a Muslim or an infidel."
4204,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Uhud, the Prophet (PBUH) ordered about Sayyidna Hamza (RA) that his dead body was placed in the direction of the Qiblah, then seven takbirs were recited over him, and other martyrs were also gathered around him until the Prophet (PBUH) prayed over him seventy times. They have been desecrated.' So he said: If I had cursed the Quraysh, I would cut thirty of their men to pieces in the same way. So Allah revealed this verse: ""If they have punished you, then you should treat them the same as you have been treated."" The narrator of this tradition is Abdul Aziz bin Imran Zaeef."
4205,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that on the day of the Battle of Uhud, Sayyidna Hamza (RA) came to the Prophet (SAW) and his lips, nose, ears, etc. were cut off and mutilated. Then Sayyiduna Hamza was given a shroud as a shroud. When his head was covered, his feet were visible. These words of the hadith have been narrated only by the narrator named Uthman: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer of any martyr other than him. These words are not preserved."
4206,"The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, these words are added in it: 'Azhar (grass) was placed on their feet and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform the funeral prayer for any martyr except him."
4207,"Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The person who was martyred in Uhud was not bathed, he was buried with his blood and his funeral prayer was not performed."
4208,"Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: I will be a witness to these people on the Day of Resurrection. Then they were buried along with their blood under the order of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). The Prophet (PBUH) did not offer their funeral prayers. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4209,"Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the polytheists left those who were killed in the Battle of Uhud and went back, the Prophet (PBUH) saw something that caused him great pain. He would have left the same, 'Until Allah the Exalted would have revived them from the stomachs of beasts and birds,' I will replace them with the likeness of seventy men. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for his cloak and covered Sayyidna Hamzah’s face with it. Sayyidna Hamzah’s feet appeared. The Prophet covered his face and placed grass on his feet. 'Even the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over them seventy times because the number of martyrs of the Battle of Uhud was seventy.' When these people were buried and you were done with it, this verse was revealed: ""Invite to the path of your Lord through wisdom and good preaching."" So the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) acted patiently and did not imitate any person. This hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Ismail bin Ayyash and there is confusion in the traditions he has quoted from narrators other than the Syrians."
4210,"Al-Khajri bin Zayd narrates this statement of his father (Zayd bin Thabit, may God be pleased with him): Earlier, people of every nation used to become heirs to each other, except when a person died blind due to the collapse of a house or a fire, or a war or any other reason."
4211,"Isa bin Harith narrates that the brother of Shareeh bin Harith had a mother-son, she gave birth to a girl, then the girl got married, she gave birth to a boy, then the mother died. It is not, because this woman is Kanwasa. So Maysara bin Yazid rode to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair and told him about what Qazi Shareeh had given a decision. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair wrote a letter to Qazi Shareeh, 'Maysara bin Yazeed has mentioned to me that you recited this verse in such a situation: ""Relationships inherit each other in the book of Allah"" This verse is about relatives and belongs to the time when people used to make an agreement with each other (i.e. they used to say: they used to become brothers) the man used to say: you become my heir and I will become your heir' When this verse was revealed, this practice was abandoned. Then Maysara bin Yazid came to Qazi Shareeh with that letter. After reading it, he refused to withdraw his decision and said: This man freed this mother in her womb (because of the child)."
4212,"Imam al-Shaabi narrates: Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: A person who kills by mistake or on purpose does not become an heir (to the slain), Allah knows best."
4213,"Amro bin Shuaib narrates his grandfather's statement regarding his father that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: The person who makes a contract of writing in exchange for one suwa qiya and pays everything except ten oqiyah, then that person will be considered a slave. will be)."
4214,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When a person who has entered into a contract of writing commits a crime or becomes a sharer in an inheritance, he will have the right to inherit according to the amount of his freed share, and according to the amount of his freed share, the limit will be issued on him."
4215,"Saeed bin Abu Saeed Maqbari narrates this with reference to his father: A woman belonging to Banulith bought me for seven hundred dirhams in the market of Zul Mijaz, then when I came, she entered into a contract with me for forty thousand dirhams. I will not take it like this, but I will take it every month or every year. I took it with me to Sayyiduna Umar and mentioned this in front of him. Sayyiduna Umar said: You deposit it in Baitul-Mal. Then Sayyiduna Umar called this woman and said: Your wealth is deposited in Baitul-Mal. Abu Saeed is free. The narrator narrates: It was sent to him, so he received it."
4216,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: The person who has entered into a contract of writing will pay the free man's dowry according to the amount he has become free, and the slave will pay the dowry according to the amount of his slave."
4217,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had given a decision regarding a person who had been killed, that according to the amount he had paid out of the contract of his correspondence, his dues would be the dues of a free person and the remaining payment would be the dues of a slave."
4218,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever has a share in a slave Yakinis and frees his share, then it is obligatory on him to free him from the shares of the remaining owners of the slave Yakinis. It will be valued according to justice and he shall pay for it on behalf of his partners according to the value of the share of the slave. But this is only when the property of the freedman is equal to the value of the shares of his partners."
4219,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever frees his share of a common slave, then the value of that slave will be assessed according to justice, and then that person will pay his other partners, and the slave will be freed by that person if he is prosperous."
4220,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: If a slave is jointly owned by two men, one of them frees his share. The narrator named Hisham has adapted it and he did not mention that this slave will be made to work. Shuba and Hisham are more hafiz than other opinions in quoting traditions regarding Qatadah. While other narrators have narrated with regard to Qatadah that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered labor, I believe that these narrators are delusional because this tradition is different from the tradition narrated by Shu'ba and Hisham."
4221,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the same tradition regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that this is the same tradition as narrated by Shu'ba."
4222,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A man freed his share of a slave, and the Prophet (PBUH) justified his freeing and ordered him to pay the remaining value of that slave as ransom. Qatadah says: If a person does not have wealth, then this slave will be made to work, but he will not be subjected to labor in this regard. Shaykh Nishapuri has stated that the best hadith is the one narrated by Hammam and he has clarified the difference between the saying of the Holy Prophet and the saying of Qatadah."
4223,"Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace be upon him) was asked about a slave that is jointly owned by two men. One of them frees his share. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That part of the slave will be freed and a suitable price will be paid from the property of the person who freed it. He will not be subjected to labor."
4224,"Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: “Whoever frees a part of his slave, then the remaining part of that slave should also be freed from that person’s property, if that person has enough wealth, otherwise, the value of that slave will be set according to justice, and then he will be made to work for it.” However, he will not be subjected to hardship."
4225,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, which is about a slave who is jointly owned by some people and one of them frees his share, then the person who freed him must also free the remaining share. And that slave will be considered free by that person. A narrator has also mentioned the maids in this tradition."
4226,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Whoever frees his share in a slave, he will be the guarantor of his freedom."
4227,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that a person came, his name was Salih, and he brought his brother. He said: O Messenger of God! I want to free this brother of mine, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you became the owner of him, then Allah freed him. A narrator Al-Azrami has been declared obsolete by Abdullah bin Mubarak, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan, Ibn Mahdi, while a narrator named Abu Nazr Muhammad bin Saib Kalbi is obsolete."
4228,"Sayyidna Muqal bin Yasar (RA) says: When you buy a slave who has been freed, he will free him without imposing this condition because it is a bond of slavery."
4229,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: If a man's slave-girl gives birth to a child, that slave-girl will be considered free after that person's death."
4230,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When someone's slave girl gives birth to his child, she will be free after that person's death."
4231,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said this: A slave girl who gives birth to a child will be considered free, even if the child is born incomplete."
4232,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A slave girl who gives birth to her master's child is automatically freed after the master's (death)."
4233,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the mother of Sayyidna Ibrahim (RA) gave birth to him, the Prophet (PBUH) said that her child has set her free."
4234,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: The mother of Ibrahim has been freed by her child."
4235,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyida Mariya (RA) gave birth to (Sayyidna Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet (PBUH), the Prophet (PBUH) said: Her child has given her freedom."
4236,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: When a slave girl gives birth to her master's child, then when that master dies, she is freed. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When Sayyida Mariya Quptiyah (RA) gave birth to Sayyidna Ibrahim (RA), the son of the Prophet (PBUH), the Prophet (PBUH) said: Her child has set her free."
4237,"He said: and 'Abd al-Hamid ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, [saying]: Abu Bakr ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Sabrah al-Qurashi narrated to me, from Husayn ibn 'Abdullah, from 'Ikrimah, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: When Mariyah al-Qibtiyyah gave birth to Ibrahim, the son of the Prophet ﷺ, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Her child has set her free."""
4238,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4239,"This tradition is narrated along with another document."
4240,"Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this."
4241,"Bashir bin Saeed narrates that Khawat bin Jubeer narrated this: A man left a will to her. This person left behind a mother and a free wife. There was a dispute between the woman and the mother of the son, so the free woman sent a message to the mother of the son: You will soon be sold. Sayyidna Khawat bin Jubeer (RA) presented this matter to the Prophet (PBUH) and he (PBUH) said: He said: He cannot be sold. Under the order of the Holy Prophet, he was declared free."
